# HapNav pin-side sensor pipeline knobs.

menu "HapNav sensors"

config HAPNAV_DROPOFF
	bool "Run the down-ToF drop-off (cliff) detector"
	default y
	help
	  Toggles the down-pointing-VL53L1X residual check that raises
	  HAPNAV_OBS_FLAG_DROPOFF when the floor slant range jumps clear of
	  a slow-tracked baseline for several consecutive frames. The slow
	  baseline tracks gradual slopes (inclines/declines) so only step
	  changes — a cliff edge, a missing step — actually fire.

	  Disable (=n) for bench-demo builds where the down ToF's geometry
	  is meaningless (the pin doesn't sit at chest height above a real
	  floor). Combined with CONFIG_HAPNAV_DOWN_TOF=n the down sensor is
	  also skipped at init so it doesn't ride the I²C bus for nothing.

	  The wristband's DROPOFF override (the all-4 square wave) takes
	  precedence over the urgency knocks, so a stuck-on drop-off cue
	  blocks the lateral-obstacle feel. With this disabled,
	  HAPNAV_OBS_FLAG_DROPOFF is never set and the wristband shows
	  urgency knocks cleanly.

config HAPNAV_HEAD_TOF
	bool "Enable the head-clearance VL53L1X sensor"
	default y
	help
	  When disabled (=n), pin_sensors_init() skips bring-up of the head
	  VL53L1X and pin_sensors_sample() leaves head_distance_mm = -1
	  permanently. The HAPNAV_OBS_FLAG_HEAD_OBSTACLE flag is therefore
	  never raised, and the wristband never sees the head-clearance
	  pattern.

	  Useful for bench demos where the VL53L5CX alone is wide enough
	  (±22.3° per axis) to cover the 10–20 cm working volume.

config HAPNAV_DOWN_TOF
	bool "Enable the down-pointing VL53L1X sensor"
	default y
	help
	  When disabled (=n), pin_sensors_init() skips bring-up of the down
	  VL53L1X (mux ch2) and the down-pointing dropoff detector is muted.

	  The down ToF only makes geometric sense in the worn pose (pin
	  upright at chest, ~1.35 m above the floor, sensor pointing forward
	  and ~45° down). In bench mode the desk's ~5 cm of clearance gives
	  meaningless slant ranges; disable then.

	  CONFIG_HAPNAV_DROPOFF must also be enabled for the dropoff flag to
	  actually fire; this knob only controls whether the down sensor is
	  brought up and polled.

config HAPNAV_BENCH_MODE
	bool "Bench-demo geometry (sensor sits on a desk)"
	default n
	help
	  Compresses the obstacle / drop-off / head-clearance distance
	  constants so the full pipeline can be exercised on a desktop with
	  the chest pin standing UPRIGHT on a desk — the VL53L5CX optical
	  centre then sits ~ 1–2 cm above the surface and grazes along it —
	  and objects moved within a 10–50 cm envelope.

	  Concretely:
	    SENSOR_HEIGHT_M         1.35 m → 0.015 m
	    FLOOR_BAND_HIGH_M      -1.20 m → -0.005 m  (desk plane = floor)
	    HEAD_TOP_BAND_M         0.40 m → 0.10 m
	    MIN_RANGE_MM             300   →   50
	    MAX_RANGE_MM            3000   →  500
	    CLUSTER_DELTA_MM         200   →   30
	    HEAD_PROXIMITY_MAX_MM   2200   →  150
	    dropoff predicted-range  3.5 m →  0.5 m
	    STATIONARY var threshold raised so the resting pin doesn't mute
	    everything (the worn pin's natural body sway re-enables it for
	    free in real-world builds).

	  Disable for the worn / real-world build. CONFIG_HAPNAV_BENCH_MODE
	  is loud at boot (the obstacle pipeline init log calls it out) so
	  it should be obvious from a UART capture which mode a binary was
	  built in.

config HAPNAV_HABITUATION
	bool "Fade alerts for obstacles stationary relative to the pin"
	default y
	help
	  Per azimuth bin, an obstacle whose nearest range holds within a
	  small deadband is treated as stationary w.r.t. the pin and its
	  urgency decays toward a floor over ~2-3 s, so a parked obstacle
	  stops nagging. Any range change beyond the deadband (the object
	  moved, or the pin moved toward/away from it) snaps urgency back
	  to full.

	  Disable (=n) to alert on every in-range obstacle regardless of
	  motion — useful for A/B comparison. The deadband, decay rate and
	  floor are compile-time constants in obstacle.c; HABIT_DEADBAND_MM
	  is the main sensitivity knob (wider = less sensitive to small
	  movements).

endmenu
